    "consumerAuditNotes": [
        "TutorialGroupImportExport creates/deletes a course, configures groups, looks up a tutor and exercises registration import and CSV/JSON export. Include account/core, automatic group communication and the lecture service used by tutorial management; retain conservative exam coverage for the shared course lifecycle. ExerciseSplitPanelResize also creates and participates in a modeling exercise for the narrow flush-panel contract.",
        "Exam workflows use ExamExerciseGroupCreationPage.addGroupWithExercise (dynamic ExerciseType dispatch) and ExamParticipationPage. Conservatively cover all exercise types and assessment for the entire exam group, including nested test-exam specs.",
        "Exercise creation/management/participation uses shared exercise services, result/assessment handling and automatic communication channels. Communication includes all such workflows plus lecture/exam and course messaging workflows.",
        "Lecture consumers include atlas competency progress/lecture links, course tabs/management/rich message editor, Iris chat/context/activity feeds, and account deletion cleanup.",
        "Quiz/programming/modeling/text/fileupload cover exam group dispatch, exercise imports and course management/tabs/context selection. Iris context selectors consume course exercise collections even when a spec only seeds one type.",
        "Atlas includes competency selectors in exercise forms, lecture unit linking and course tab/date picker workflows. CompetencyContributionComponent actively calls CourseCompetencyService from non-quiz CourseExerciseDetailsComponent panels and expanded LectureUnitComponent cards (Atlas is enabled in the CI core profile). Audit direct student exercise routes, ProgrammingExerciseOverviewPage.startParticipation callers (including admin/FeatureUsageGit and localci/KubernetesLocalCI), and lecture-unit expansion; quiz-only panels, empty lectures and empty exercise lists do not mount that component. Assessment includes exam/test-exam results and presentation assessments.",
        "Core/account/security/bootstrap/shared/runtime changes remain full suite. Global module names in specModules document owners but do not authorize selective changes to global source paths.",
        "Course setup/cleanup and overview endpoints are used across domains; the course contract deliberately includes all application workflows. Pure helper contracts retain their own owners.",
        "Review direct request paths, named runtime operations and dynamic workflow helpers when maintaining this contract. fixtures.ts exposes many lazy fixtures; importing that bag does not consume every module.",
        "Routed client dependencies matter even without direct test API calls: tutorialgroup detail/overview inject LectureService; atlas details/edit/create and course-competency service consume LectureUnitService/LectureService; communication message-editor resources/suggestions load lectures. Their owner workflows are lecture consumers.",
        "IrisSettingsService/IrisChatService are injected by lecture views, programming participation/editor, atlas learning-path views and communication tutor-suggestion/redirect components. Conservatively select these owner workflows for Iris changes, even when the current CI profile hides chat UI.",
        "CourseOverviewComponent (course/overview/course-overview/course-overview.component.ts) unconditionally subscribes to ExamParticipationService.examIsStarted$; its template uses the emitted state for sidebar visibility and layout. courses.route.ts mounts this parent for all student /courses/:courseId children. Specs visiting those routes directly or through audited course/programming/competency pageobjects are exam consumers; management-only routes do not inherit this parent.",
        "The opt-in exam-management-client exact-file mapping replaces only the broad exam mapping for its three audited files. Its consumers include the entire quiz UI group because quiz-question-list-edit-existing.component.ts actively loads accessible exams when shown. Passive service injection in course-only assessment/grading/user-import/archive branches does not subscribe to exam state or execute exam HTTP calls; their exam-context paths are covered by the exam group. Mixed scoped and broader exam inputs union both scopes. This is a maintained runtime contract, not a general guarantee for exam/manage/.",
        "CourseManagementTumUi creates and deletes users, manages course membership, configures grading and team forms, and creates/submits/assesses a real modeling exercise. Conservatively retain course-management server/module consumers plus core account lifecycle and modeling/assessment. It does not consume the exact exam-management client override. Shared UI/package inputs keep the existing full-suite fallback."
    ],
